  "note": "Triennial election; the polling day was Thursday 15 January 1914. On Monday 5 January James Lennon, town clerk, received exactly six nominations for each ward, so \"there won't be any contest in Armagh this year, and it is expected that all nominated candidates will be declared elected on Tuesday\" (the Armagh Guardian, 9 January 1914, p. 3: \"No City Election this Year\"). The paper calls this ward St. Mark's Ward (the East Ward of 1905 and 1911). No Nationalists were nominated. Irwin and Maxwell are styled J.P., Anderson solicitor and Parkinson C.E."
